  "sequence": "Pinned source/full-bird and era sources first, before reviewer reports; then all 3-era canon-neutral/workshop whole pairs and head details, selected native opposite/rear/profile views; then paired saved browser captures; only after my image pass read three raw final reports and frozen comparison. No current report claims were consulted before first image judgment.",
  "first_pixel_judgment": "The inherited source has a visibly layered, irregular and patinated crown with dark optic recesses. Loop03 reads as a slightly cooler/more integrated plate against the retained assembly, but its crown is still broad and smooth; the native whole views do not show an obvious compensating source-construction or era-specific gain. Initial concern: small tonal gain may be outweighed by reduced crown finish variation/source distinction.",
  "falsifiers": [
    {
      "id": "F1_source_finish_tradeoff",
      "challenge": "Loop03 lowers mottled/brushed crown variation or collapses Builder/Maker/Mechanic finish differences enough that its small tonal integration cannot justify the loss.",
      "condition_that_would_prove_objection_wrong": "In source-first paired whole views, across each era and both lights, crown tonal integration is visibly improved while source-like era differences and useful surface variation remain legible; the residual smooth plate mismatch remains local and less consequential at whole size.",
      "actual_test": "Pinned Sept22 full-bird source and Maker/Mechanic era sources; all six Loop02/Loop03 canon-neutral and canon-workshop whole pairs, plus paired head-neck details in all three eras.",
      "result": "Partially survives as a limitation but does not overturn the small development gain: Loop03 slightly cools and quiets the crown versus Loop02; it does not reproduce pinned layered/riveted crown/crest or convincingly add the three distinct source finishes. At whole size it remains local and does not erase era distinctions elsewhere; no sufficiently large cost found to negate tiny tonal integration. This does not establish whole-character source alignment.",
      "decision_implication": "Retain only as small local appearance progress with crown texture/shape and era differentiation still open."
    },
    {
      "id": "F2_opposite_rear_angle_or_emphasis",
      "challenge": "The crown improvement fails from opposite/rear/eight-angle views or diminishes edge/optic emphasis enough to offset whole-view benefit.",
      "condition_that_would_prove_objection_wrong": "Paired opposite/profile/rear/eight-angle views in neutral and workshop show no meaningful continuity loss, while front/opposite views preserve crown edge and optic contrast.",
      "actual_test": "Actual paired Builder neutral 000/090/180/270 and workshop 090/180; plus paired 000/090/180/225 neutral per era had been visually reviewed before this task\u2019s angle pass (previous own-pass summary). Across selected views change stays on forward top panel; at side it is subtle, at rear panel is occluded and rear silhouette/stance unchanged. Head details and front whole views preserve optic ring/edge contrast.",
      "result": "Objection not supported at tested angles. Crown tone shift remains slight in side/opposite views, absent on rear; no visible edge or optic emphasis loss. Not all 8 angles/both lights were reopened in this pass; no claim of exhaustive angular validation.",
      "decision_implication": "No new angle-specific blocker identified; underlying mismatched crown construction persists."
    },
    {
      "id": "F3_browser_delivery_visibility",
      "challenge": "The claimed appearance gain is native-only, disappears in browser delivery, or only changes highlights.",
      "condition_that_would_prove_objection_wrong": "Matched saved Loop02/Loop03 browser screenshots across all three eras in neutral and exhibit modes, including fallback image states and reset, visibly retain the same small crown tonal shift and whole-size readability.",
      "actual_test": "Viewed all 12 saved Loop02 and 12 Loop03 browser captures: builder/maker/mechanic \u00d7 neutral, exhibit, fallback-neutral, fallback-exhibit. Compared shared camera/reset whole-character canvas.",
      "result": "Gain survives in the saved browser captures across all three eras and both lighting modes; fallback states likewise show the cooler/lower-contrast crown. It is not merely a native-render artifact. Screenshots show static review page/canvas state; this is not fresh browser interaction nor pixel parity. Native and browser lighting/shaders differ, so appearance magnitude differs.",
      "decision_implication": "Sufficient to reject disappearance-only objection for captured states; still no live browser orbit/mobile/runtime certification."
    }
